  {
   "what": "object gain is dropped by both encoders",
   "evidence": "all five gain-varied objects come back with gain 0 in the metadata and with their essence at the authored level; the total tone power is the same, -23,02 dBFS, for the object authored at 0 dB and for the one authored at -24 dB. The encoded bitstream itself carries gain Db(0): `oadec emdf --dump 1` on the E-AC-3 encode reads it straight out of the OAMD payload, before any of this decoder's DAMF writing.",
   "whose behaviour": "the encoder"
  },
  {
   "what": "object size is rendered into the spatial coding, not carried",
   "evidence": "the metadata comes back with size 0 in both codecs, and the object is spread: a point source is carried by one element, size 0,25 by seven, size 0,5 by eight and size 1,0 by eleven. The total tone power is within 0,3 to 1,2 dB of the authored level, so the spreading loses almost nothing. The element the spread object is loudest in reports a position at the room edge rather than the authored one, which is what a spread across the room gives.",
   "whose behaviour": "the encoder"
  },
